SUPPLEMENTAL TERMS — COMMERCIAL USE AND THE PRO / ENTERPRISE EDITIONS

These terms are offered by the licensor alongside the PolyForm Noncommercial
License 1.0.0 above. They are not part of that licence and do not modify it.
Where they grant you something, they grant it in addition.

1. What you may do at no cost

   Everything the licence above permits. Concretely: run the studio and the
   CLI, generate and validate datasets, read and modify the source, port it,
   fork it, publish your changes, write papers about it, teach with it, and
   use it inside a charity, school, university, public research body or
   government institution — regardless of how that institution is funded.

2. What requires a commercial licence

   A separate written commercial licence from the licensor is required to:

     a) sell, resell, rent, sublicense or otherwise distribute this software
        or any derivative of it for a fee, including repackaging it under
        another name or brand;

     b) offer it, or a derivative of it, as a paid or ad-supported product or
        service, hosted or otherwise, including as part of a larger offering;

     c) use it to produce datasets, reports or attestations in the course of
        commercial activity, whether or not the output is sold; or

     d) remove, replace or obscure the Required Notice above.

   Nothing in this section restricts what the law already allows you to do
   without permission, including fair use.

3. The Pro and Enterprise editions

   The source of every feature, including the reporting and attestation layer,
   is in this repository and is covered by the licence above. What the Pro and
   Enterprise editions add is the ENTITLEMENT to use that layer, granted by a
   licence key the licensor issues:

     - signed provenance declarations that a third party can verify offline
       (Ed25519 attestation over the generated dataset), and
     - the executive PDF audit report.

   Those capabilities are gated in the software and are unlocked only by an
   official licence key. Keys are issued solely through the licensor's
   Lemon Squeezy store:

       https://ai-synthetic-data-studio.lemonsqueezy.com/checkout/buy/
       17400e93-40b9-47d9-aee2-9eaa676964a0

   A key is issued to the named purchaser, is limited to the seat count it
   carries, and is governed by these terms together with the purchase terms
   shown at checkout. Keys are not transferable and may be revoked if the
   underlying payment is reversed.

4. Licence keys and the enforcement code

   You may read, audit and modify the licence and provenance code — that is
   the point of publishing it. You may not, however, distribute a build or a
   derivative that forges, bypasses, disables or misrepresents the licence
   check in order to obtain or offer the Pro or Enterprise capabilities
   without a valid key, nor generate, share or sell keys or tokens that
   imitate ones the licensor issues. Doing so is use outside your licences
   under the terms above.

   Studying the mechanism, testing it against your own keys, and reporting
   weaknesses to the licensor are expressly permitted.

5. Verification is free for everyone, always

   Checking a signed dataset or report that someone else produced never
   requires a licence, a key, a payment or a network connection. An auditor
   receiving a signed file must always be able to verify it independently, and
   the licensor will not restrict that.

6. Third-party components

   Dependencies keep their own licences, which are unaffected by these terms.

